==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|vetur|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vetr||winter, year|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*wintruz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvɛːtʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːtʏr|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|vetrar|vetur}}

# [[winter]], [[wintertime]]
#: '''''Veturinn''' er loksins kominn!''
#:: '''Winter''' has finally arrived!
#: '''''Vetur''' er í [[nánd]]''
#:: '''Winter''' is close.
# [[year]] (counting age)
#: ''Barnið er fimm '''vetra''' gamalt.''
#:: The child is five '''years''' old.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-vetur}}

====Derived terms====
* [[fimbulvetur]]
* [[í vetur]] (this winter)
* [[á veturna]]/[[á vetrin]] (in [[winter]], in the winter)
* [[í vetur sem leið]] (last winter)

